## Habitica

There's a gated bridge in Apps Script. It can create `claude`-tagged todos and read
progress. It **cannot** delete, edit, or complete anything — the allowlist is enforced in
the only function that touches the network, so nothing routes around it. Quest queue
lives in Drive as `quests <date>`; `-` lines become Habitica checklist items.

If you touch it: dry run defaults to ON when the flag is missing, receipts are mandatory,
and the audit is written in a `finally` block. Those three exist because each was missing
once and it cost something.

